<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's CMVM to lift suspension CPP shares.</title>
<headline>Portugal's CMVM to lift suspension CPP shares.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Financial Markets Committee (CMVM) has decided to lift a suspension in shares of bank Credito Predial Portugues (CPP) at 1000 GMT, a CMVM official said.</p>
<p>Yesterday the Champalimaud group announced a public offer to buy (OPA) for CPP, a unit of Champalimaud's Banco Totta e Acores, at a price of 1,800 escudos per share.</p>
<p>CPP closed yesterday at 2,075 escudos per share.</p>
</text>
